{
    "_about": "Phrases that are actions, not words to search for, the same in every shop: 'הכי זול' sorts by price, 'במבצע' keeps what is on sale, 'גדול מ-2' keeps what is bigger than 2. Read in code on the server and in the browser alike (HebrewSearch::actions and readActions), first match of each entry, in this order; comparisons come before the bare 'גדול' and 'קטן'. Patterns are case-insensitive regular expressions matched as whole words; a group captures the number. An entry that needs 'size' is left out in a shop with no size attribute (search.size_attribute), so its words stay words there. A shop's own vocabulary values ('זהב צהוב') are not here: they stay words, and are offered as filters beside the results. 'או' between words searches each side (HebrewSearch::either).",
